    "updated_at": "2026-11-10T01:22:22Z",
    "body": "Checked against the contributor's Tormach manuals (2026-11-09):\n- **UM10753 8L manual, §3.1:** confirms X 4.5\" (114 mm), Z 10\" (with tailstock), 180-2500 / 350-5000 rpm, 150 IPM. This settles the web knowledge base's conflicting 10\" X.\n- **UM10225 15L Slant-PRO manual, §1.1:** confirms X 10\", Z 12\", 60 IPM rapid, 15\" swing, 180-2500 rpm (6\" chuck) / 250-3500 rpm (5C). It gives **3 hp continuous**, so the draft's 1.1 kW (1.5 hp) is wrong and the corrected figure is 2.24 kW, fixed on the branch.\n- **Tool holding:** the 15L offers a manual quick-change post, a gang plate or the 8-position turret. The file states the turret's 8, and a QCTP or gang shop can raise it.\n- **Not included:** the 15LX (UM10860) and the PCNC Duality lathe attachment are separate machines and can follow on request.",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "pin": null,
